<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20360" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hĕlĭcē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλίκη</span> (a winding). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of slender</i>, <i>flexible
				willow</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 37, 69, §
			177</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			As <i>nom. propr.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hĕlĭcē</span></b> . </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The constellation of the Great Bear</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 20, 66</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3,
				108</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 17</span></i>.— <b>Transf.</b>, <i>the North</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Grat. Cyneg. 55</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet.
			1539</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A maritime town of Achaia</i>, <i>swallowed up by the sea</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15,
				293</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 92, 94, § 206</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 23, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
